# Python Type Hints
Use modern Python typing (3.9+):
- Built-in generics: list[T], dict[K, V], set[T]  
- Union types with |: str | None, int | float
- Optional values: x | None (not Optional[x])
- Type aliases: use = directly (TypeAlias not needed)
- Match collection types to stdlib names: list not List
- Avoid from typing import *
- Only import specific types if no built-in equivalent
Keep type hints clean, minimal and readable.
Validate with mypy --strict.